{"name":"Ambassador Blue","hex":"#0d2f5a","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ambassador","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A diplomat of the highest rank sent to a foreign court to represent there their sovereign or country. (Sometimes called ambassador-in-residence)","An official messenger and representative."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ambassador"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ambassador","blocks":[{"text":"An ambassador is an official envoy, especially a high-ranking diplomat who represents a state and is usually accredited to another sovereign state or to an international organization as the resident representative of their own government or sovereign; or appointed for a special and often temporary diplomatic assignment. The word is also used informally for people who are known, without national appointment, to represent certain professions, activities, and fields of endeavor, such as sales."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ambassador","wikidata":"Q121998"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Ambassador_%28Persia%29.jpg/500px-Ambassador_%28Persia%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Ambassador_%28Persia%29.jpg/500px-Ambassador_%28Persia%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ambassador Daoud Zadour of Persia.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAmbassador_(Persia).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Accademia_-_Arrivo_degli_ambasciatori_inglesi_presso_il_re_di_Bretagna_di_Vittore_Carpaccio.jpg/500px-Accademia_-_Arrivo_degli_ambasciatori_inglesi_presso_il_re_di_Bretagna_di_Vittore_Carpaccio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Accademia_-_Arrivo_degli_ambasciatori_inglesi_presso_il_re_di_Bretagna_di_Vittore_Carpaccio.jpg/1280px-Accademia_-_Arrivo_degli_ambasciatori_inglesi_presso_il_re_di_Bretagna_di_Vittore_Carpaccio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Accademia_-_Arrivo_degli_ambasciatori_inglesi_presso_il_re_di_Bretagna_di_Vittore_Carpaccio.jpg/500px-Accademia_-_Arrivo_degli_ambasciatori_inglesi_presso_il_re_di_Bretagna_di_Vittore_Carpaccio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Arrival of the English Ambassadors by Vittore Carpaccio, painted between 1495 and 1500—though ostensibly part of a series of paintings on the life of Saint Ursula, this actually depicts the developing diplomatic practices of the Republic of Venice in the painter's own time.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAccademia_-_Arrivo_degli_ambasciatori_inglesi_presso_il_re_di_Bretagna_di_Vittore_Carpaccio.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/AmbassadorSchwarz%2CBush.jpg/500px-AmbassadorSchwarz%2CBush.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/AmbassadorSchwarz%2CBush.jpg/1280px-AmbassadorSchwarz%2CBush.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/AmbassadorSchwarz%2CBush.jpg/500px-AmbassadorSchwarz%2CBush.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Before an ambassador takes office, their credentials must be accepted, such as when South African Ambassador Harry Schwarz handed his credentials to U.S. President George H. W. Bush in 1991.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAmbassadorSchwarz%2CBush.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Maria-Pia_Kothbauer_with_Vaclav_Klaus.jpg/330px-Maria-Pia_Kothbauer_with_Vaclav_Klaus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Maria-Pia_Kothbauer_with_Vaclav_Klaus.jpg/330px-Maria-Pia_Kothbauer_with_Vaclav_Klaus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Maria-Pia Kothbauer, Princess of Liechtenstein and ambassador extraordinary and plenipotentiary to the Czech Republic, presenting her credentials to Václav Klaus.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMaria-Pia_Kothbauer_with_Vaclav_Klaus.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedi